{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSdvmvMbow13hwHDvyWY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the codebase, here's what I found:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that cancels active orders, persists an order status field (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), validates that no CONFIRMED shipments exist, prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders, and idempotently succeeds when cancelling already-cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11-16): No status field currently\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27): In-memory, basic CRUD\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:15-46): Create and Get endpoints\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9-27): Already has ShipmentStatus enum\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27): No method to find by orderId\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:20-56): Creates shipments\n- API exceptions (ApiExceptions.kt:11-30): ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, etc.\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28): Converts exceptions to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Errors are thrown as ApiException subclasses that specify status and ErrorCode\n- Controllers throw exceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError JSON\n- Tests use MockMvc with @BeforeEach reset and jsonPath assertions for both status and error code\n- Status codes: 201 CREATED, 200 OK, 404 NOT_FOUND, 409 CONFLICT\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — add `status: OrderStatus` field, create OrderStatus enum\n2. OrderController.kt — add POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with cancellation logic\n3. OrderRepository.kt — add `findByOrderId` method to query shipments (actually belongs in ShipmentRepository)\n4. ShipmentRepository.kt — add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` to check for CONFIRMED shipments\n5. ShipmentController.kt — add check in create() to reject shipments for CANCELLED orders\n6. ApiError.kt — add ORDER_CANCELLED error code for shipment rejection\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt — add tests for all cancel scenarios\n8. ShipmentControllerTest.kt — add test for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- All-or-nothing atomicity: must not partially cancel shipments and then fail\n- Thread safety: concurrent updates to Order and Shipment statuses\n- Status initialization: existing test setup must initialize orders as ACTIVE\n- Error codes: ORDER_CANCELLED is new and becomes part of the API contract\n\n**Open questions:** None that change correctness; the ticket is explicit.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Modify `Order` data class to include `status: OrderStatus` field. Modify `CreateOrderRequest` to not include status (it's always ACTIVE on creation).\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — No changes needed; existing `save` and `findById` are sufficient.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - Throws ConflictException with error code ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - If already CANCELLED, succeeds and returns the order unchanged\n   - If ACTIVE, changes to CANCELLED, updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, saves order, returns order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the `create()` method, after checking for duplicate shipment ID, fetch the order and check if it's CANCELLED. If so, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED error code.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Add two new error codes to ErrorCode enum:\n   - ORDER_CANCELLED (for rejecting shipment creation)\n   - ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED (for rejecting cancel if CONFIRMED shipment exists)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order succeeds, returns order with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel an already CANCELLED order succeeds with no change\n   - Cancel fails with 409 if order has CONFIRMED shipment and order stays ACTIVE\n   - Cancel fails with 404 for non-existent order\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add one test case:\n   - Creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order fails with 409 and ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered having the cancel endpoint also handle creating shipments (no separate check needed in ShipmentController), but that would couple the shipment logic to the order cancel flow. Keeping the check in ShipmentController is better because it makes the shipment creation rule independent and testable.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE, no CONFIRMED | Order | Order (CANCELLED), Shipments (CREATED→CANCELLED) | 200 Order | Response.body + saved |\n| Cancel ACTIVE, has CONFIRMED | Order, Shipment | (nothing) | 409 ConflictException | Thrown, caught by GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Cancel CANCELLED | Order | (nothing) | 200 Order | Idempotent success |\n| Cancel not found | (nothing) | (nothing) | 404 ResourceNotFoundException | Thrown |\n| Create shipment, order CANCELLED | Order | (nothing) | 409 ConflictException | Thrown |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **OrderControllerTest#cancelActiveOrder** — Create order, call cancel, assert 200, CANCELLED status, shipments updated\n- **OrderControllerTest#cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent** — Cancel twice, second succeeds, no change\n- **OrderControllerTest#cancelFailsIfConfirmedShipmentExists** — Set up order with CONFIRMED shipment (via repository), cancel returns 409, order stays ACTIVE\n- **OrderControllerTest#cancelNonexistentOrderReturns404** — Call cancel on non-existent order\n- **ShipmentControllerTest#createShipmentForCancelledOrderFails** — Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, assert 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes. I'll start with the Order entity to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":22162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1097},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d384686-b713-4360-b336-7c76bc72759b","uuid":"596189d5-d35a-4e90-a124-8b9aa38beae0","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:54:56.866Z","request_id":"req_011CfSdvmYYNN9ekmbRMfeKy"}
