{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSe522Qa21W3wdtotMKW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 19 tests passed. Let me review the changes made:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — Build succeeded with 19 tests passing (4 new order tests, 1 new shipment test, others unchanged)\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 19 tests passed including the baseline tests\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's CREATED shipments** — OrderControllerTest#cancelActiveOrder and #cancellingAnActiveOrderCancelsItsCreatedShipments verify this\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses existing ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) pattern\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — Covered by:\n   - OrderControllerTest#cancellingAnAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent\n   - OrderControllerTest#cancelFailsWithErrorIfOrderHasAConfirmedShipment\n   - OrderControllerTest#cancelReturns404ForNonExistentOrder\n   - ShipmentControllerTest#rejectsCreatingAShipmentForACancelledOrder\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — No pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified order, shipment, and api modules\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order data class with default ACTIVE. This is necessary and sufficient.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED error codes. Both are new but minimal additions to the error contract.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order ID. Necessary for cancel logic to check for CONFIRMED shipments.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Added cancel() endpoint with:\n   - 404 if order not found ✓\n   - 200 if already CANCELLED (idempotent) ✓\n   - 409 if any CONFIRMED shipment exists (atomic, no changes) ✓\n   - 200 if ACTIVE, transitions to CANCELLED, cascades to CREATED shipments ✓\n   - Injected ShipmentRepository to check shipment statuses ✓\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added check in create() to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders with 409. Injected OrderRepository for order status check.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 5 new test cases covering all cancel scenarios including idempotency and cascade behavior.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test case for rejecting shipment creation on cancelled order.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are addressed and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement** — Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders with status tracking (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), idempotently succeeds for already-cancelled orders, rejects if any shipment is CONFIRMED (409, no changes), and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Changed**\n- Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order\n- ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED error codes\n- ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order ID\n- OrderController.kt — Added POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with full cancellation logic\n- ShipmentController.kt — Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 5 tests: cancel active order, idempotent cancel, confirmed shipment blocks cancel, non-existent order, cascade to created shipments\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 1 test: shipment creation on cancelled order rejected\n\n**Tests**\n- OrderControllerTest#cancelActiveOrder — Verifies cancel transitions order to CANCELLED and returns 200\n- OrderControllerTest#cancellingAnAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent — Verifies second cancel succeeds without change\n- OrderControllerTest#cancelFailsWithErrorIfOrderHasAConfirmedShipment — Verifies 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n- OrderControllerTest#cancelReturns404ForNonExistentOrder — Verifies 404 for missing order\n- OrderControllerTest#cancellingAnActiveOrderCancelsItsCreatedShipments — Verifies CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED\n- ShipmentControllerTest#rejectsCreatingAShipmentForACancelledOrder — Verifies 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED when order cancelled\n\n**Verification** — Ran `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ directory. Result: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 19 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n**Not done** — Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no files outside scope modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3318,"cache_read_input_tokens":36466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3318},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d384686-b713-4360-b336-7c76bc72759b","uuid":"37e87fb1-c6cf-4a9a-8c8e-44212516a627","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:56:38.862Z","request_id":"req_011CfSe51X9APX166GG4G9Pd"}
